// C: awk classifies each variable name as scalar or array while parsing the whole
// program (tran.c / awkgram.y), then rejects a scalar assignment to a name that's
// used as an array anywhere else — e.g. `j = 4` followed later by `"x" in j` fails
// with "can't assign to j; it's an array name.", regardless of statement order.
// This walks the parsed AST once, up front, to reconstruct that global classification.

